Modified native Burger assembly and differential wheel drive to remove Linux ROS
dependencies. Added a rigid tandem constraint, keyboard and local UDP control.
Original Burger Blueprint, meshes and physical materials are copied unchanged.
RR2DLidarComponent now adapts upstream ray geometry to synchronous ideal range
scans, excluding the full tandem from self hits. Noise, intensity response and
ROS publishing are not ported. This is not a full Rapyuta/ROS port.
The original script module and content mount names are retained for asset references.

Added Windows-native RGB scene capture and ideal chassis IMU measurements.
These use Unreal rendering/rigid-body state and a local UDP interface, not the
upstream ROS publishers or a calibrated commercial camera/IMU noise model.
